<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept corn imports down 11.9 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept corn imports down 11.9 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's corn imports fell by 11.9 percent in September from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Tuesday. Details were as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>			September 96  August 96     September 95</p>
<p> Total		1,206,777     1,277,819     1,371,007</p>
<p> Feed corn total    772,056	 744,155	 823,247</p>
<p> others		 434,721	 533,664	 547,760</p>
<p> Top supplier of feed corn (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		   748,333	 717,776	 806,209</p>
<p> Argentina		9,595	  10,707	  17,038</p>
<p> China		    5,090	   5,227	     nil</p>
<p> South Africa	   8,038	   7,393	     nil</p>
<p> Australia		1,000	   3,052	     nil</p>
<p>Imports in the first nine months of this year totalled 11,703,936 tonnes against 12,343,868 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
</text>
